# q2-usbtrace trace format (docs/internals.md#usb-tracer), built from a device log for test/unit/test_usb_fsm.py.
# Source: car1129/logs/q2-usb.log lines 337 to 700, 2026-11-23, V1SSi (demo ms as s; dmesg's uptime is demo + 4.052),
# the AB13X earbuds the night docs/internals.md#otg-host-power tells: the laptop's cable out at 989.412, four seats
# that held PD17 low with no source (usb/online 0; the no-source lines), and two that brought PD18 low, each powered by
# stock's 6 s settle, enumerated, and cut once the device left (otg-off why=gone). The pin trace's lines are 250 ms
# apart, so the times below are samples, not edges. Not in the record: when each no-source seat's PD17 went low (put
# 2 s before its no-source line, OTG_NO_SOURCE_MS) and, for the first two, when it went high (1112.0 put between them)
# [I]; the second device's removal is dmesg's "usb 1-1: USB disconnect" at 1193.270 (demo 1189.218).
